  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Integration of Mental Health and Psychosocial support and Non-Communicable Diseases Prevention and Care in Humanitarian Response</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">As the full-scale war is approaching one-year mark, the crisis has affected millions of Ukrainians and led to a multitude of stressors and challenges that are often difficult to cope with. The war is taking a heavy toll on the mental health condition of millions of people, requiring an urgent increase in mental health and psychological support.  In addition to primary humanitarian needs, this rehabilitation program of Faith, Hope, Love necessarily includes a psychological component, namely, crisis counseling, the removal of acute conditions, stabilization, and, if necessary, accompaniment by a multidisciplinary team (psychologist, psychiatrist, neurologist).</narrative>
  </description>
